    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, the equity part is a big one. I've seen some people calling it a \"regressive tax\" that just hits regular workers harder, but then I also see a lot of experts saying it's one of the most effective tools we actually have to hit climate targets and fix transit. In your experience as a consultant, does the environmental/transit benefit usually outweigh those economic concerns, or is it more of a wash?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
