      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As a consultant, the balance is rarely absolute, as each side has strong, valid points. The strongest models suggest that when properly designed with robust rebate or exemption programs, the positive environmental and transit benefits can significantly outweigh the regressive tax perception. However, if the pricing mechanism is poorly implemented, the economic burden can disproportionately affect vulnerable populations.",
      "source": "target",
